      "start_line": 4,
      "end_line": 10,
      "numbered_excerpt": "4|Post-hoc sensitivity analysis of the primary outcome with various methods of imputation for\n5|missing data\n6|A post-hoc sensitivity analysis of the primary outcome (see table further) showed that the LOCF results were\n7|similar to 3 other imputation methods: linear interpolation, maximum likelihood analysis (no case wise deletion\n8|by SAS Proc Mixed), and Markov chain Monte-Carlo (MCMC) multiply imputation that is suitable for arbitrary\n9|missing patterns. This comparison showed that the BTX-A clinical efficacy was invariant whatever the method\n10|of imputation used.",
