      "page": 15,
      "start_line": 9,
      "end_line": 15,
      "numbered_excerpt": "9|LOCF is one of the different methods of imputation that can be applied to datasets containing few missing data.\n10|In the present study, out of 1650 data points for weekly pain (primary outcome) (66 x 25 records) only 131\n11|(7.9 %) were missing, and out of 396 data points (66 x 6 visits), 29 (7.3 %) were missing. Because they were\n12|more prevalent at the end of the 24 weeks period mostly due to dropouts (time effect, Friedman test: p<0.0001)\n13|and more prevalent in the placebo group (2-sample Wilcoxon test: p=0.043) the missing pattern was identified as\n14|Missing at Random (MAR). No baseline effect on the missingness was detected, thereby ruling out a Missing\n15|Not at Random (MNAR) pattern.",
      "numbered_excerpt_sha256": "710a5d923c39b699cd989ff2ab1198b0444ed7e55e78a00c1bb799f451a26b29",
