      "numbered_excerpt": "58|13 (38%) of 34 participants in the botulinum toxin A\n59|group correctly identifi ed their treatment group at the\n60|last visit of participation in the study (ie, week 24 or\n61|earlier) solely on the basis of the improvements\n62|experienced, 15 (44%) thought they had received placebo\n63|because they felt no improvement, and six (18%) did not\n64|know. 17 (53%) of 32 participants in the placebo group\n65|thought they had received placebo because of an absence\n66|of improvement, eight (25%) did not know, and seven\n67|(22%) thought they had received botulinum toxin A\n68|because of improvement. None of the participants who\n69|correctly identifi ed their active treatment stated that this\n70|was because of skin modifi cations or injection pain.\n71|Similarly, none of the investigators who did the\n72|assessments noticed any skin modifi cations after\n73|botulinum toxin A.",
